        "ec_numbers": [
          "2.3.2.27"
        ],
        "function": [
          "E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase which is a component of the N-end rule pathway (By similarity). Recognizes and binds to proteins bearing specific N-terminal residues that are destabilizing according to the N-end rule, leading to their ubiquitination and subsequent degradation (By similarity). In complex with ced-3, required for the ced-3-mediated cleavage and subsequent degradation of the heterochronic protein lin-28 to regulate seam cell fate patterning during larval development (PubMed:28602583). Negatively regulates glutamate metabolism through the aspartate aminotransferase got-1.2 (PubMed:29649217). Modulation of glutamate levels most likely controls locomotory behavior, in particular backwards locomotion or 'reversals' (PubMed:29649217)."
        ],
